course: dictionary
lesson: 15775
title: Tusked: animals with long teeth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a thing by what it has. «The tusked boar dug up roots with its snout.» You can see the word tusked, and the rest of the sentence tells you what a boar does: it digs with its snout. Digging is one job tusks are used for, so tusked must be about tusks.
explain: Tusks are long, pointed teeth that stick out of the mouth. «The elephant's tusks were long and white.» Elephants, walruses, wild boars and narwhals all have tusks. Tusked means having them, so a tusked animal has tusks.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit. In «The tusked monster roared in the dark forest», the word tusked tells you the monster has long teeth sticking out, which makes it sound fierce. Then try your meaning in the sentence: "The boar with long teeth sticking out dug up roots." It still makes sense, so you have it.
fact: Tusked means having tusks.
fact: Tusks are long, pointed teeth that stick out of the mouth.
fact: Animals with tusks include elephants, walruses, wild boars and narwhals.
fact: Tusks are used for digging, fighting, lifting and showing off.
fact: Phrases you may see are «a tusked boar», «tusked mammals» and «long-tusked».
exercise: «The tusked boar dug up roots with its snout.» What does tusked mean here? | Covered in thick, soft fur | Having a very long, thin tail | *Having long, pointed teeth that stick out of the mouth | Able to swim very fast
exercise: Which of these animals is tusked? | A rabbit | A goldfish | A butterfly | *A walrus
exercise: Which word means having tusks? | scaly | sharp | *tusked | hairy
test: Which phrase describes a wild boar with long teeth? | *a tusked boar | a silent owl | a hungry bird | a wet pond
test: What are tusks? | *Long, pointed teeth that stick out of the mouth | The tail of a bird | Short, soft whiskers | A kind of feather
exam: Which one is not tusked? | *a rabbit | a walrus | an elephant | a wild boar
